1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,517
A quantum dot sits between two electrodes.

2
00:00:02,757 --> 00:00:05,550
Apply a bias across them,
and electrons tunnel

3
00:00:05,569 --> 00:00:08,362
through one after another,
carrying a current.

4
00:00:08,917 --> 00:00:11,802
At large bias the system
is far from equilibrium

5
00:00:11,822 --> 00:00:15,130
and equilibrium Green's
functions are no longer enough.

6
00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:19,310
We need a different tool:
the Keldysh nonequilibrium Green's function.

7
00:00:20,567 --> 00:00:26,246
This video follows a classic set of lecture notes,
starting from equilibrium perturbation theory

8
00:00:26,266 --> 00:00:30,164
then building up contour Green's functions,
the Langreth rules and

9
00:00:30,184 --> 00:00:34,972
the Keldysh equation, and finally computing
the current through a resonant level.

10
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:37,550
Let's start with equilibrium.

11
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:42,142
The zero-temperature single-particle
Green's function is a time-ordered

12
00:00:42,162 --> 00:00:45,898
correlation of two field operators
in the exact ground state.

13
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:49,583
The trouble is that it requires
the exact ground state

14
00:00:49,603 --> 00:00:52,022
which is precisely what we cannot compute.

15
00:00:53,283 --> 00:00:55,825
The fix is to work in
the interaction picture

16
00:00:55,845 --> 00:00:58,500
with an S-matrix,
which obeys a group property.

17
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:02,586
Then we switch the interaction on slowly,
starting in the infinite past.

18
00:01:02,826 --> 00:01:06,379
By the Gell-Mann and Low theorem,
the noninteracting ground

19
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:09,710
state evolves adiabatically
into the true ground state.

20
00:01:10,266 --> 00:01:11,772
The crucial step comes next.

21
00:01:12,012 --> 00:01:17,337
In equilibrium, if we slowly switch the
interaction off again in the infinite future

22
00:01:17,357 --> 00:01:21,345
the system returns to its original
ground state, up to a phase.

23
00:01:21,585 --> 00:01:24,310
So the bra can also be
obtained with the S-matrix

24
00:01:24,330 --> 00:01:26,382
coming back from the infinite future.

25
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:32,933
Now the Green's function is an expectation
value in the noninteracting ground state.

26
00:01:33,173 --> 00:01:37,668
Expand the S-matrix, contract the
operators pairwise with Wick's theorem

27
00:01:37,688 --> 00:01:43,561
and you get Feynman diagrams, with the disconnected
ones cancelled exactly by the denominator.

28
00:01:44,817 --> 00:01:48,100
Out of equilibrium, though,
this crucial assumption fails.

29
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:52,916
Nothing forces the system back to where it started,
not even in the infinite future.

30
00:01:53,484 --> 00:01:56,968
Think of an atom hitting a surface
and exchanging charge with it

31
00:01:56,988 --> 00:02:01,130
the state it leaves in is completely
different from the state it arrived in.

32
00:02:02,384 --> 00:02:05,749
The way out is to never refer
to the infinite future at all.

33
00:02:05,989 --> 00:02:09,341
Start from the known initial state,
evolve forward in time

34
00:02:09,361 --> 00:02:12,598
to the moment we care about,
and then evolve back again.

35
00:02:13,167 --> 00:02:15,980
Every expectation value is then defined with

36
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,557
respect to a well-defined initial state.

37
00:02:18,797 --> 00:02:23,063
The price is that the two time branches
must be treated on an equal footing.

38
00:02:23,303 --> 00:02:24,713
This is the Keldysh contour.

39
00:02:25,267 --> 00:02:28,047
This closed loop also buys
us something for free.

40
00:02:28,287 --> 00:02:31,339
Going forward and then
back again is the identity

41
00:02:31,359 --> 00:02:35,102
so the evolution around the
whole contour multiplies to one.

42
00:02:35,342 --> 00:02:38,246
The awkward denominator
of the equilibrium theory

43
00:02:38,266 --> 00:02:41,470
and with it all the vacuum bubbles,
simply disappears.

44
00:02:42,034 --> 00:02:45,670
At the initial time the system
is in thermal equilibrium

45
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:50,306
and the thermal density matrix itself
is an evolution in imaginary time

46
00:02:50,326 --> 00:02:53,898
so the full contour also
carries an imaginary-time leg.

47
00:02:54,138 --> 00:02:57,710
If we push the initial time to
the infinite past and switch

48
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:01,303
the interactions on adiabatically,
this leg can be dropped.

49
00:03:01,543 --> 00:03:03,878
The price is losing initial correlations

50
00:03:03,898 --> 00:03:06,705
which usually does not
matter for steady states.

51
00:03:07,967 --> 00:03:11,511
On the contour, we replace time
ordering by contour ordering

52
00:03:11,531 --> 00:03:14,362
and define the contour-ordered
Green's function.

53
00:03:14,917 --> 00:03:18,286
Remarkably, the topological
structure of perturbation

54
00:03:18,306 --> 00:03:21,164
theory is exactly the
same as in equilibrium.

55
00:03:21,404 --> 00:03:25,728
The contour Green's function obeys
a Dyson equation of the same form

56
00:03:25,748 --> 00:03:29,498
except that every time integral
now runs along the contour.

57
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:35,718
Each of the two time arguments can sit on
either the forward or the backward branch

58
00:03:35,738 --> 00:03:40,300
so the contour function contains four
real-time functions: the time-ordered

59
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:44,455
the anti-time-ordered,
the greater and the lesser Green's functions.

60
00:03:45,817 --> 00:03:49,691
They obey one identity,
so only three are linearly independent.

61
00:03:49,931 --> 00:03:53,612
The most convenient choice is
the lesser and greater functions

62
00:03:53,632 --> 00:03:56,299
together with the retarded
and advanced ones.

63
00:03:57,667 --> 00:04:00,978
Retarded minus advanced
equals greater minus lesser.

64
00:04:01,219 --> 00:04:04,766
Intuitively, the lesser function
describes occupied states

65
00:04:04,786 --> 00:04:09,686
the greater function describes empty states,
and the difference between retarded

66
00:04:09,706 --> 00:04:13,623
and advanced gives the spectral function,
the density of states.

67
00:04:14,884 --> 00:04:17,999
Here is the deeper reason we
need this extra function.

68
00:04:18,239 --> 00:04:20,656
The retarded function tells us which states

69
00:04:20,676 --> 00:04:23,094
exist and how long they live: the spectrum.

70
00:04:23,334 --> 00:04:27,123
The lesser function tells us how full
those states are: the occupation.

71
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:32,621
In equilibrium, the two are locked together
by the fluctuation-dissipation theorem

72
00:04:32,641 --> 00:04:36,611
the lesser function is just the
Fermi function times the spectrum.

73
00:04:36,851 --> 00:04:38,630
Out of equilibrium that lock breaks.

74
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:43,824
The same spectrum can be filled in a completely
different way, set by kinetics instead

75
00:04:43,844 --> 00:04:48,452
of temperature, and that is exactly the
information the lesser function carries.

76
00:04:49,717 --> 00:04:52,230
But the Dyson equation lives on the contour

77
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,941
while in the end we want
real-time quantities.

78
00:04:55,181 --> 00:04:57,793
The key tool for this step
is the Langreth theorem.

79
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:01,428
Take a convolution of two
functions on the contour.

80
00:05:01,668 --> 00:05:05,072
Put the first time on the forward
branch and the second time on

81
00:05:05,092 --> 00:05:08,388
the backward branch,
so what we want is its lesser component.

82
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:12,120
Now deform the integration
contour into two pieces

83
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:16,523
one looping around the first time,
and one looping around the second.

84
00:05:17,084 --> 00:05:21,089
On the first piece, the integration
variable always comes earlier on

85
00:05:21,109 --> 00:05:24,877
the contour than the second time,
so B becomes a lesser function

86
00:05:24,897 --> 00:05:28,903
while the two parts of A combine
into exactly the retarded function.

87
00:05:29,143 --> 00:05:32,359
The second piece gives an advanced
function in the same way.

88
00:05:33,617 --> 00:05:36,844
The result is beautifully tidy:
C lesser equals A

89
00:05:36,864 --> 00:05:40,556
retarded times B lesser,
plus A lesser times B advanced.

90
00:05:40,796 --> 00:05:46,029
Products of three functions work the same way:
the lesser label slides along the chain

91
00:05:46,049 --> 00:05:50,427
with retarded functions to its left
and advanced functions to its right.

92
00:05:50,667 --> 00:05:55,469
The retarded component is even simpler,
just the product of the retarded functions.

93
00:05:56,834 --> 00:05:58,901
There is a simple picture behind this rule.

94
00:05:59,141 --> 00:06:02,610
Think of the product as a path
that starts on the forward branch

95
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:06,973
the history of the ket, and ends on the
backward branch, the history of the bra.

96
00:06:07,213 --> 00:06:11,990
It has to switch branches exactly once:
links before the switch are retarded

97
00:06:12,010 --> 00:06:16,156
the link that switches is lesser,
and links after it are advanced.

98
00:06:16,396 --> 00:06:19,305
Summing over where the switch
happens gives the three terms.

99
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:22,357
These rules fit into a single table.

100
00:06:22,597 --> 00:06:26,378
As a demonstration,
deriving the retarded electron-phonon

101
00:06:26,398 --> 00:06:29,379
self-energy with them
takes just a few lines.

102
00:06:30,633 --> 00:06:34,213
Now apply the Langreth rules to
the Dyson equation on the contour

103
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:37,258
and we get an equation for
the lesser Green's function.

104
00:06:37,816 --> 00:06:42,142
Iterating it to all orders gives the
Keldysh equation: a first term that

105
00:06:42,162 --> 00:06:46,730
depends on the initial state,
and a second term that is the retarded Green's

106
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:51,196
function times the lesser self-energy
times the advanced Green's function.

107
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:56,234
For a steady state, if the system was
noninteracting in the infinite past

108
00:06:56,254 --> 00:06:59,503
the first term vanishes and
only the second survives.

109
00:06:59,743 --> 00:07:03,389
Note that this is still an integral equation,
because the lesser

110
00:07:03,409 --> 00:07:07,169
self-energy usually depends on the
lesser Green's function itself.

111
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:10,694
This equation has a transparent meaning.

112
00:07:10,934 --> 00:07:13,506
The lesser self-energy is the rate at which

113
00:07:13,526 --> 00:07:16,037
the leads inject electrons at each energy.

114
00:07:16,277 --> 00:07:20,756
The retarded and advanced functions
then carry each injected electron

115
00:07:20,776 --> 00:07:24,668
along until it leaks away again,
so the occupation is simply

116
00:07:24,688 --> 00:07:28,840
the injection rate times the time
an electron dwells on the dot.

117
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,598
And the first term,
the memory of the initial state, fades away.

118
00:07:33,838 --> 00:07:37,276
Start the dot with any occupation you like:
it relaxes

119
00:07:37,296 --> 00:07:42,077
on the time scale h-bar over Gamma,
to the steady value fixed by the leads.

120
00:07:42,317 --> 00:07:45,494
After a few lifetimes the
initial state is forgotten

121
00:07:45,514 --> 00:07:48,137
which is why only the second term survives.

122
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:52,805
Now for the application:
mesoscopic tunneling structures.

123
00:07:53,045 --> 00:07:56,397
A central region sits between
a left and a right electrode.

124
00:07:56,967 --> 00:07:59,862
In the remote past,
the three parts are decoupled

125
00:07:59,882 --> 00:08:03,432
each in thermal equilibrium with
its own chemical potential.

126
00:08:03,672 --> 00:08:06,466
The two chemical potentials
can differ by a lot

127
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:08,861
with no need to be close to equilibrium.

128
00:08:09,417 --> 00:08:12,557
Then the tunneling couplings
between them are switched on

129
00:08:12,577 --> 00:08:15,939
and handled by perturbation
theory on the two-branch contour.

130
00:08:16,179 --> 00:08:20,249
The couplings need not be weak,
and typically must be summed to all orders.

131
00:08:21,417 --> 00:08:23,762
The Hamiltonian splits into three parts

132
00:08:23,782 --> 00:08:26,915
the contacts, the tunneling,
and the central region.

133
00:08:27,155 --> 00:08:29,948
The contacts are
noninteracting electron gases.

134
00:08:30,188 --> 00:08:33,076
The central region can be
a set of simple levels

135
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:37,620
or include electron-phonon coupling,
or an Anderson-type Coulomb repulsion.

136
00:08:38,883 --> 00:08:43,401
The current is the rate of change of the
electron number in the left electrode.

137
00:08:43,641 --> 00:08:47,811
After working out the commutator,
it can be written as the lesser component

138
00:08:47,831 --> 00:08:51,888
of a mixed Green's function between
the electrode and the central region.

139
00:08:52,450 --> 00:08:56,253
Because the nonequilibrium theory
is structurally equivalent to the

140
00:08:56,273 --> 00:09:00,190
equilibrium one, we only need the
zero-temperature equation of motion

141
00:09:00,210 --> 00:09:03,842
continued onto the contour with
the Langreth rules, to integrate

142
00:09:03,862 --> 00:09:07,436
out the electrodes and leave a
current that depends only on the

143
00:09:07,456 --> 00:09:11,430
central-region Green's functions and
the level-width functions, Gamma.

144
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:15,615
For a single level,
this formula reads like a ledger.

145
00:09:15,855 --> 00:09:19,870
Electrons flow in from the left
at rate Gamma L whenever the lead

146
00:09:19,890 --> 00:09:23,656
state is filled and the dot state is empty,
and flow back out

147
00:09:23,676 --> 00:09:27,442
whenever the dot state is filled
and the lead state is empty.

148
00:09:27,682 --> 00:09:31,007
Subtract the two,
the Pauli blocking factors cancel

149
00:09:31,027 --> 00:09:33,892
and what remains is exactly this expression.

150
00:09:34,132 --> 00:09:37,621
These are the same rates that will
reappear in the master equation.

151
00:09:38,783 --> 00:09:42,555
If the left and right couplings
are proportional to each other

152
00:09:42,575 --> 00:09:48,793
the current formula collapses into a strikingly simple form:
the difference of the two Fermi functions

153
00:09:48,813 --> 00:09:52,768
times an effective transmission function,
integrated over energy.

154
00:09:54,033 --> 00:09:58,856
Current flows only inside the bias window,
where the two Fermi functions differ.

155
00:09:59,096 --> 00:10:02,979
And the transmission is set by the
difference between the retarded and

156
00:10:02,999 --> 00:10:06,938
advanced Green's functions,
which is essentially the density of states.

157
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:13,179
Picture two streams at every energy:
electrons coming from the left with weight f L

158
00:10:13,199 --> 00:10:17,847
and from the right with weight f R,
each getting through with probability T.

159
00:10:18,087 --> 00:10:22,371
Deep below both chemical potentials
the two streams cancel exactly.

160
00:10:22,612 --> 00:10:25,348
Only inside the window
does a net flow survive.

161
00:10:25,916 --> 00:10:28,751
This formula holds for
interacting systems too.

162
00:10:28,991 --> 00:10:31,517
But how useful it is
depends on whether we can

163
00:10:31,537 --> 00:10:34,504
actually compute the
central-region Green's functions.

164
00:10:35,767 --> 00:10:39,135
The simplest example is a
single noninteracting level.

165
00:10:39,375 --> 00:10:43,757
The imaginary part of the retarded
self-energy is half the level width

166
00:10:43,777 --> 00:10:46,651
so the spectral function
is a Lorentzian peak.

167
00:10:47,217 --> 00:10:49,874
The stronger the coupling,
the broader the peak

168
00:10:49,894 --> 00:10:53,920
the shorter the electron stays on the dot,
the less certain its energy.

169
00:10:55,484 --> 00:10:56,144
Here is why.

170
00:10:56,384 --> 00:11:00,358
Put an electron on the dot at time zero:
its amplitude oscillates

171
00:11:00,378 --> 00:11:04,536
at the level energy while leaking
into the leads, so the probability

172
00:11:04,556 --> 00:11:08,469
of still finding it decays as e
to the minus Gamma t over h-bar.

173
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:12,730
The Fourier transform of that
decaying oscillation is exactly

174
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:16,772
a Lorentzian of width Gamma:
a short life means a broad line.

175
00:11:17,934 --> 00:11:20,990
The lesser self-energy is a
weighted mix of the left and

176
00:11:21,010 --> 00:11:24,177
right Fermi functions,
weighted by the coupling strengths.

177
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:28,063
So the dot is occupied as if
it sat in a pseudo-equilibrium

178
00:11:28,083 --> 00:11:31,233
distribution,
blended from the two Fermi functions.

179
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,024
There is a neat way to see this blend.

180
00:11:34,264 --> 00:11:38,771
Each lead keeps resetting the dot:
lead alpha does so at rate Gamma alpha

181
00:11:38,791 --> 00:11:42,059
and leaves the state filled
with probability f alpha.

182
00:11:42,299 --> 00:11:47,058
So the dot simply copies the Fermi
function of whichever lead touched it last

183
00:11:47,078 --> 00:11:51,528
and lead alpha was the last one with
probability Gamma alpha over Gamma.

184
00:11:52,684 --> 00:11:55,848
The current is the transmission
times the difference

185
00:11:55,868 --> 00:11:58,727
of the Fermi functions,
integrated over energy.

186
00:11:58,967 --> 00:12:02,508
And here the transmission is
exactly a Breit-Wigner Lorentzian.

187
00:12:03,067 --> 00:12:04,987
Two facts hide inside this Lorentzian.

188
00:12:05,227 --> 00:12:09,436
At resonance, with symmetric barriers,
the transmission reaches one

189
00:12:09,456 --> 00:12:12,403
two barriers that are
each nearly opaque become

190
00:12:12,423 --> 00:12:16,381
perfectly transparent together,
just like a Fabry-Perot cavity.

191
00:12:16,621 --> 00:12:21,103
And the plateau current scales as
Gamma L times Gamma R over their sum

192
00:12:21,123 --> 00:12:25,606
like two resistors in series,
so the weaker barrier is the bottleneck.

193
00:12:26,767 --> 00:12:28,159
Now slowly raise the bias.

194
00:12:28,399 --> 00:12:30,566
As the level enters the bias window

195
00:12:30,586 --> 00:12:34,129
the current rises quickly,
then saturates into a plateau.

196
00:12:34,369 --> 00:12:38,237
The width of the step is set by both
the temperature and the level width.

197
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:42,986
The same problem can also be
handled with a master equation.

198
00:12:43,226 --> 00:12:47,496
The dot has only two states: empty,
or occupied by one electron.

199
00:12:48,050 --> 00:12:52,310
Electrons hop in from the electrodes at some rate,
and hop back out at another.

200
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:56,252
The rates come from Fermi's golden rule,
proportional to the

201
00:12:56,272 --> 00:13:00,223
probability of finding an electron,
or a hole, in the electrode.

202
00:13:01,483 --> 00:13:05,721
In the steady state, the occupation
probability is a weighted average

203
00:13:05,741 --> 00:13:09,917
of the two Fermi functions,
and the current takes a simple form too.

204
00:13:11,083 --> 00:13:15,284
In the weak-coupling limit,
the Lorentzian shrinks into a delta function

205
00:13:15,304 --> 00:13:19,505
and the Green's function result agrees
exactly with the master equation.

206
00:13:19,745 --> 00:13:24,352
But once the level width is comparable
to the temperature, the master equation

207
00:13:24,372 --> 00:13:28,564
is no longer accurate,
while the Green's function result remains exact.

208
00:13:29,733 --> 00:13:33,603
The difference is sharpest when the
level sits outside the bias window.

209
00:13:33,843 --> 00:13:37,730
The master equation then only
allows thermally activated current

210
00:13:37,750 --> 00:13:41,454
which dies off exponentially
with the distance to the window.

211
00:13:41,694 --> 00:13:45,121
The Green's function keeps the
Lorentzian tails of the level

212
00:13:45,141 --> 00:13:50,004
so current still leaks through by quantum tunneling,
falling off only as a power law.

213
00:13:51,167 --> 00:13:55,110
The notes close by sketching how the
master equation could be derived

214
00:13:55,130 --> 00:13:58,039
from the equations of motion
in the wide-band limit

215
00:13:58,059 --> 00:14:02,404
and invite the reader to spot a few
suspicious approximations along the way.

216
00:14:03,667 --> 00:14:04,291
To sum up.

217
00:14:04,850 --> 00:14:09,071
Out of equilibrium, the system does
not return to its initial state

218
00:14:09,091 --> 00:14:13,187
so we evolve forward and then
backward along the Keldysh contour.

219
00:14:13,750 --> 00:14:17,592
Contour Green's functions obey
a Dyson equation with the same

220
00:14:17,612 --> 00:14:21,454
structure as in equilibrium,
and the Langreth rules translate

221
00:14:21,474 --> 00:14:25,190
it into retarded,
advanced and lesser real-time components.

222
00:14:25,750 --> 00:14:28,823
The Keldysh equation gives
the lesser Green's function

223
00:14:28,843 --> 00:14:31,917
and from it the current
through an interacting region.

224
00:14:32,157 --> 00:14:35,617
For a resonant level it yields
Breit-Wigner transmission

225
00:14:35,637 --> 00:14:38,849
and reduces to the master
equation at weak coupling.

226
00:14:39,417 --> 00:14:44,459
Behind every formula sits one physical picture:
the leads inject electrons

227
00:14:44,479 --> 00:14:47,607
the electrons propagate
with a finite lifetime

228
00:14:47,627 --> 00:14:52,875
and the occupation that results is set
by kinetics, not by temperature alone.

229
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:56,244
Master these few steps,
and you have the skeleton

230
00:14:56,264 --> 00:14:58,901
of the nonequilibrium
Green's function method.

231
00:14:59,141 --> 00:14:60,000
Thanks for watching.
